{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexSubstitutionScale","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexSubstitutionScale","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35TraceClosedForm"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.substitutionRateFactor_denominator_vanishes_numerator_does_not","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.substitutionRateFactor_denominator_vanishes_numerator_does_not","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/WeakVertexSubstitutionScale.lean#L85-L95","doc":"**Why the factor has no classical limit** — the fact that retired the \"order derived\"\nbridge of bean `qou-q2l7`. At `q = 1` the denominator vanishes while the numerator does\nnot: `s²(1) = 0` but `W(1)² = 1/16`. So `|W|²/s^k` diverges as `q → 1` for every `k ≥ 1`,\nand no finite constant is its leading value — in particular the `−96` of\n`couplingRatio_one` is the leading value of `(J − 1)/s²`, a *different* ratio, whose\nnumerator vanishes because `V_K(1) = 1` for every knot. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.substitutionRateFactor_near_one_hundred_thirty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.substitutionRateFactor_near_one_hundred_thirty","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/WeakVertexSubstitutionScale.lean#L73-L83","doc":"**The negative, checked at the proton pin, at the corrected power.** At\n`q₀ = 1.1099785` the factor lies in `(129, 130)`: the substitution multiplies every decay\nrate by about `129`, shortening every predicted half-life by two orders of magnitude. Far\ntoo large to be the `10–17 %` correction the corpus attributed to it, so the scope-(a)\nnegative stands — at `129×`, not the `1.19·10⁴` this file claimed until 2026-09-05\n(bean `qou-xql6`). Stated as a two-sided band on the measured value, not a round window. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.substitutionRateFactor_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.substitutionRateFactor_eq","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/WeakVertexSubstitutionScale.lean#L65-L71","doc":"Closed form of the factor: `q⁵ (q¹² + q⁸ − 1)² / ((q² + 1)⁴ (q − 1)²)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.substitutionRateFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.substitutionRateFactor","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/WeakVertexSubstitutionScale.lean#L59-L63","doc":"The rate-scaling factor of the prescribed substitution, `|W|²/s²`, as a rational\nfunction of `q`. **One** power of `sSq`: the rate carries the single-crossing amplitude\nsquared exactly once, and `sSq` *is* that square (see the corrected note above). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.sSq_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.sSq_eq","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/WeakVertexSubstitutionScale.lean#L53-L57","doc":"`s² = q + q⁻¹ − 2`: the square-root form and the rational form agree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.sSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.WeakVertexT35.sSq","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/WeakVertexSubstitutionScale.lean#L49-L51","doc":"The single-crossing coupling `s² = (q^{1/2} − q^{-1/2})² = q + q⁻¹ − 2 = (q − 1)²/q`,\nwritten without the square root. ","signatureChunk":0}]}